The QA test file imports `calculate_dimensions` from `xarray.core.variable`. In `test_dimensions_repeat_determinism_part_a`, it creates one `variables` mapping and calls `calculate_dimensions(variables)` inside `for _ in range(5)`, so the same input is used five times. The function itself initializes new local dicts each call, then walks each variable’s `dims` and `shape` to fill a dimension-size mapping, raising only on conflicts. With `"a"` shaped `(2, 3)` over `("x", "y")` and `"b"` shaped `(3,)` over `("y",)`, every call computes the same result `{"x": 2, "y": 3}`. Because the function is deterministic for this unchanged input, the output is identical across all five executions.

